    <section class="wp-page" id="page-1">

      <div class="wp-page-num">PAGE 01</div>

      <h2>The Laugh That Wanted More</h2>

      <div class="wp-emoji-hero">😂</div>

      <p>
        Meme culture is one of the most powerful social forces
        of the internet age. It brings strangers together,
        creates inside jokes between people who will never
        meet, and turns shared laughter into a language of its own.
      </p>

      <p>
        But there is a question almost nobody asks:
        <strong>what if that same energy could do something more?</strong>
      </p>

      <p>
        Today, meme culture is measured in engagement, virality,
        and attention — but rarely in impact. Millions of people
        laugh together every day, and then they move on.
        The laughter happens. Nothing else does.
      </p>

      <p>
        ChucklePad exists because we think that's a waste.
      </p>

      <div class="wp-quote">
        People should not have to choose between having fun
        and doing something meaningful.
      </div>

      <p>
        <strong>ChucklePad ($CPAD)</strong> combines meme
        culture, community participation, education,
        rewards, and social impact in one place — designed so
        that every laugh, and every challenge quietly feeds into
        something larger than itself.
      </p>

      <p>
        The philosophy is simple: <strong>little by little.</strong>
        Just built, one honest step at a time.
      </p>

      <p>
        This white paper explains what ChucklePad is,
        why it exists and how it works.
      </p>

    </section>


    <section class="wp-page" id="page-2">

      <div class="wp-page-num">PAGE 02</div>

      <h2>The Ecosystem That Laughs Back</h2>

      <p>
        ChucklePad is a small ecosystem of interconnected experiences —
        each one designed to reward presence, effort, and community.
      </p>

      <div class="wp-cards">

        <div class="wp-card">
          <div class="wp-card-emoji">🧠</div>
          <div class="wp-card-title">DAILY</div>
          <h3>Daily Hunt</h3>
          <p>One thoughtful question a day. Share a real idea. Earn Points and Tickets.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="wp-card">
          <div class="wp-card-emoji">🚀</div>
          <div class="wp-card-title">GAME</div>
          <h3>Rocket Rush</h3>
          <p>Three attempts a day. Provably fair. Cash out before the rocket explodes.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="wp-card">
          <div class="wp-card-emoji">🏆</div>
          <div class="wp-card-title">WEEKLY</div>
          <h3>Weekly Heist</h3>
          <p>Turn your tickets into a weekly score. Top 100 split a 1,000,000 Point pool.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <h3>Points and Tickets</h3>

      <p>
        Every activity earns <strong>Points</strong>. Points are
        the off-chain currency of participation — they accumulate
        in your profile, and they reflect how much you've
        contributed to the community.
      </p>

      <p>
        Daily Hunt earns <strong>Tickets</strong>.
        Tickets feed directly into the Weekly Heist — the more
        valid Hunts you complete during a Monday-to-Monday window,
        the higher you climb. At the end of each week, the top
        100 ticket holders split a <strong>1,000,000 Point pool</strong>.
      </p>

      <h3>Why Base</h3>

      <p>
        ChucklePad is built on <strong>Base</strong>, the
        Ethereum L2 incubated by Coinbase. Base is fast, cheap,
        and increasingly the home of serious on-chain
        communities. When $CPAD arrives, it will arrive on Base,
        and ChuckleGovernment NFTs will live on Base.
      </p>

