    <section class="wp-page" id="page-3">

      <div class="wp-page-num">PAGE 03</div>

      <h2>Three Pillars, One Purpose</h2>

      <p>
        ChucklePad's long-term vision is built around three
        impact pillars.
        <strong>31% of the total $CPAD supply</strong> is
        allocated directly to fund them.
      </p>

      <div class="wp-emoji-row">
        <span>🎓</span>
        <span>🌾</span>
        <span>❤️</span>
      </div>

      <h3>🎓 ChuckleScholar</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Helping make education more accessible.</strong>
        Supporting children and young people who lack essential
        educational resources — school supplies, books,
        scholarships, and educational programs.
      </p>

      <h3>🌾 ChuckleFeed</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Supporting food security through agriculture.</strong>
        Supporting agricultural communities and encouraging
        greater participation in farming and food production —
        small-scale farmers, farming supplies, youth agriculture,
        and community food initiatives.
      </p>

      <h3>❤️ ChuckleCare</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Supporting vulnerable children.</strong>
        Helping children and communities facing difficult
        circumstances — children's homes, vulnerable children,
        basic necessities, and community support.
      </p>

      <h4>WHY THIS IS STRUCTURAL, NOT SYMBOLIC</h4>

      <p>
        Many projects write a charity percentage into their
        tokenomics and never deliver. ChucklePad's commitment
        is different because:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>The allocation is written into the token contract.</li>
        <li>Release is governed by <strong>ChuckleGovernment</strong> — the community that holds the NFTs (see Page 5).</li>
        <li>Every distribution will be publicly logged with partner identification, amount, and date.</li>
        <li>No pillar funds will move without community approval.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Real impact is not a launch-day event — it is a decade-long project.
      </p>

    </section>


